2a0u|v|To be or to continue awake; to watch; not to sleep. ; To sit up late festive purposes; to hold a night revel. ; To be excited or roused from sleep; to awake; to be awakened; to cease to sleep; -- often with up. ; To be exited or roused up; to be stirred up from a dormant, torpid, or inactive state; to be active. ; To rouse from sleep; to awake. ; To put in motion or action; to arouse; to excite. ; To bring to life again, as if from the sleep of death; to reanimate; to revive. ; To watch, or sit up with, at night, as a dead body.	o:286o,37,2~286o,37,2	D:286o,53,6~286o,53,6
